From 7695bbdd29082acbb4b6f30554c6841978f3d6b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:52:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 061/114] media: i2c: add GalaxyCore GC02M1B driver

The GC02M1B is the 2 MP monochrome helper sensor of the OnePlus 9 Pro.
One 1600x1200 Y10 mode at 30 fps over a single D-PHY lane at 672 Mbps,
with the register settings from the phone's camera module data.

Gain is exposed as a linear value in 1/1024: the driver picks the
largest of the sensor's 16 analogue steps (0xb6) below it and makes up
the rest with the digital gain (0xb1/0xb2), as the vendor library does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
